In &#x201C; Elsinore ,&#x201D; Andrew Scott plays real-life actor Ian Charleson, who performed his final role while dying of AIDS.

Written by Stephen Beresford, &#x201C;Elsinore&#x201D; follows the deeply emotional and inspirational true story of Charleson as he confronts his mortality with courage, honesty and wit. On Nov. 13, 1989, Charleson walked onto the stage at London&#x2019;s National Theatre to play Hamlet for the last time. He was dying of AIDS, a fact he kept secret. Very few of the 1,000 audience members at the Olivier Theatre knew his story. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Korea Box Office: Anime Phenomenon 'Chiikawa' Staves Off Corporate Thriller 'Final Interview' to Retain Top Spot 'Cliff Booth' First Reactions: Brad Pitt's Sequel Is an ‘Absolute Triumph’ and a ‘Wildly Entertaining’ ‘Love Letter’ to Hollywood

The biopic (currently in theaters) reunites Scott with Olivia Colman , who previously starred alongside him in &#x201C;Fleabag.&#x201D; This time, their bond is a special one as Colman plays Margaret Johnson, the doctor who treats Charleson.

For &#x201C;Elsinore,&#x201D; both actors needed to transform themselves &#x2014; not only into the real people they were portraying, but also back to the 1980s. That&#x2019;s where makeup department head Nadia Stacey played a key role. Stacey, who was honored at last month's Middleburg Film Festival, spoke about her work and approach to the film, explaining that &#x201C;when there are real people, you have to be sympathetic to them.&#x201D;

Stacey described the '80s as a tricky period to recreate, given it can easily become clich&#xE9;d. &#x201C;You immediately imagine everybody had a perm,&#x201D; she said. &#x201C;My approach every time is that you shouldn't notice hair and makeup unless you actually want to notice hair and makeup. The story told itself. I just needed to tell his journey and put us in the era we were in without overdoing it.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Stacey worked to achieve a look that embodied Scott&#x2019;s portrayal of Charleson while keeping everything authentic. &#x201C;We know Andrew as that &#x2014; jet black hair and brown eyes,&#x201D; Stacey explained. Charleson, however, had blonde hair and blue eyes. &#x201C;We didn&#x2019;t want to push something too far to jar the audience. Andrew and I talked about it, and we said we should approach it in the sense of how an actor at that time would have done it. They would have been dyeing their hair themselves.&#x201D; Instead of bleaching Scott&#x2019;s hair, Stacey gave him a full head of blonde highlights and blue contact lenses, capturing Charleson's defining characteristics.

She would also track his journey after Charleson tested positive for HIV in 1986. As Charleson&#x2019;s health declined, Stacey discolored Scott&#x2019;s skin tone and added dark circles. For the sarcoma lesions, she used tattoo transfers, which she applied to Scott&#x2019;s body.

Joining Stacey for the conversation was Colman, who also underwent a transformation to play Johnson. &#x201C;The second you put a wig on someone, as an audience, you know they&#x2019;re wearing a wig. So it&#x2019;s hard to make sure that it looks good,&#x201D; Stacey said. &#x201C;I felt like we were telling a story about real people, and we needed to be as close to that as possible without pulling her out of the story. But from all the photos we had of Margaret, we know she had this blonde bob, so we tried it.&#x201D; And it worked.

Colman had also done her research on playing Johnson and knew how important it was to stay as close to the character as possible. She recalled, &#x201C;We tried on the wig in the makeup room, and because I had been watching Margaret, I was very much up for a wig.&#x201D;

Colman pointed out that the film doesn't glorify Charleson's death. Throughout the film, casting director Jessica Ronane cast background actors who actually knew him. David Rintoul &#x2014; Charleson&#x2019;s actual best friend &#x2014; plays the Ghost of Hamlet&#x2019;s father. Some of the hospital cast were also friends of the late actor.

Colman shared, &#x201C;The most interesting thing about finding out about Ian is every single person he spoke to said, 'Ian was hilarious. Ian was funny.' And so they wanted that. Everybody that they approached said, 'Absolutely. Yes, please, count me in.'&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

In the film's final act, Johnson comes to see Charleson. The camera focuses primarily on Johnson being moved by his performance. &#x201C;Andrew, bless his heart, came to be there that day. It was only on me, and they&#x2019;d already filmed the other bits, but he insisted. On a very long, exhausting shoot, on his day off, he came in and said, &#x2018;Absolutely, I&#x2019;ll do it for you.&#x2019; So he was performing bits of &#x2018;Hamlet&#x2019; for me.&#x201D;

Fast forward to the film's premiere at the London Film Festival, and Colman reflected, &#x201C;I cried as it started till the end and had to pass tissues to the person next to me as well. And I think, for me, even though I'd seen it, it was seeing him in it and what it took to do that. He's so incredible and so generous and so fun. Honestly, if I could just choose a handful of people to work for the rest of my career, he would absolutely be one of them.&#x201D;

Colman also shared the film's powerful response: "There&#x2019;s something beautiful about film reminding you of these past heroes."

In a world of increasingly short attention spans, social media slop and doomscrolling brainrot, it&#x2019;s a wonder why many television shows got longer in the streaming era.

Case in point, the 22-minute broadcast sitcom was largely replaced by the 30-minute dramedy and the 43-minute procedural has been overshadowed by the hour-long premium drama series.

Netflix , however, has found success with a much shorter concept in Minimum Wage .

The comedy series, which comes from Jeremy Garelick and Will Phelps&#x2019; American High , consists of 14 episodes between 12 and 20 minutes in its first tranche, which debuted at the end of October. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Set in a pizza joint and starring new SNL darling Grace Reiter , Aidan Micho, Hyde Healy, Julia Dicesare, Luke Burke, Ryan Micho, Tommy Armstrong and Randall Park, its short episodes are a feature, not a bug. Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

Phelps told Deadline, &#x201C;The future is these 15-minute kind of SpongeBob -length episodes where it's really fast. There's not any fat.&#x201D;

In fact, Netflix demanded short episodes for the show, which began life as a series of YouTube sketches shot during the middle of the night with interns as camera operators and a building manager handling the boom mic.

Garelick said, &#x201C;When we closed the deal, [Netflix] said that they wanted it to be a minimum of twelve and a half-minute episodes. It was an interesting challenge because most episodic TV shows are 22 to 30 pages. It was almost like we were inventing a new structure as we were going and it was hard.&#x201D;

Episodes were also capped at 20 minutes with shooting scripts ending up being around 15 pages and the cast encouraged to improv. &#x201C;You can captivate an audience for 15 minutes really well,&#x201D; Phelps added. &#x201C;Jeremy and I are coming at it from traditional screenplay writing and the cast is coming at it from making the most exciting one-minute thing for TikTok or Instagram.&#x201D;

This contrast is both the essence of Minimum Wage and also highlights one of the industry&#x2019;s challenges as creators such as Druski and others are increasingly working on scripted projects for streamers. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;Everyone&#x2019;s clamoring for creators to make shows now [following] the success of Obsession and Minimum Wage and I&#x2019;m nervous that without the guidance of traditional screenwriters, you might fall into a trap of creators that are used to taking a one-minute premise and being told expand that into 15 minutes. That's just going to be full of fat. Whereas we're taking stories that really should be a half-hour and squeezing the fat out from the other side. That's the secret sauce that we have.&#x201D;

Garelick began his career working as an assistant for Joel Schumacher and working on movies such as The Break-Up and The Wedding Ringer before teaming up with Phelps to buy a high school in upstate New York, where they made films such as Banana Split, Holly Slept Over and Pete Davidson-starrer Big Time Adolescence.

&#x201C;We've become a traditional Hollywood studio, but we give a lot more trust to the creators and the artists, and we have an academy, our shorts and our sketch teams, and we're kind of combining [it all],&#x201D; said Garelick.

This also allowed American High to deliver more episodes of Minimum Wage than Netflix had originally ordered. The streamer initially greenlit 20 episodes but they ended up writing 28 scripts and persuaded Netflix that it would be cheaper to produce them all.

&#x201C;We don't get hung up on the actual business side of things. We'll just do it for the love of the game,&#x201D; added Phelps.

Minimum Wage debuted last month and reached Netflix&#x2019;s global top ten charts with 2.4M views, impressive given the season&#x2019;s run time is under four hours.

It is one of a number of streaming shows keeping episode lengths concise. Shane Gillis&#x2019; Netflix comedy series Tires is generally in the 20-23-minute range, while HBO Max&#x2019;s The Big Bang Theory spinoff Stuart Fails To Save The Universe consists of episodes between 18 and 20 minutes with one episode clocking in at only 15 minutes.

Co-creator Chuck Lorre, who has spent the vast majority of his career working in broadcast comedy, said there was &#x201C;no real reason&#x201D; to pad the episodes . &#x201C;The historic length of a show is entirely arbitrary, it comes from network television where a certain amount of advertising has to be sold to pay the way of making this television, but it&#x2019;s not an element any longer in streaming,&#x201D; Lorre said. &#x201C;So, why not just make the best show we can and hope the audience is entertained and is not looking at their watch.&#x201D;

Minimum Wage works because it is a workplace comedy, one featuring an overwhelmed group of teenagers struggling to run The Slice Club, where the &#x201C;stakes are low and the pressure is immense.&#x201D;

It&#x2019;s not clear whether the remaining 14 episodes that American High shot will be labeled as the second part of season one or season two, but they are expected to air in spring 2027. There&#x2019;s also plenty of road for more episodes; Garelick said that they&#x2019;ve already got around 50 more draft scripts.

The pair are also developing more projects using a similar model of testing out ideas across its YouTube channels including American High Shorts, which has over 4.5M subscribers, College Life, which has over 1M subs, and Entry Level and Gurgle, USA.

&#x201C;It takes a few months to get there, and then it takes a year or so of incubating that online to get a fan base, and then you're ready to start a show with some solid footing behind it, and the audience feels like they were part of the inception of this,&#x201D; said Phelps. &#x201C;I think it's the future of TV.&#x201D;

Stephan James has played a few real-life figures in his career, including Olympic gold medalist Jesse Owens (in 2016's &#x201C;Race&#x201D;) and civil rights leader John Lewis (2014's &#x201C;Selma&#x201D;), so he knows the drill. Diving deep into the archives for research. Vocal coaching. Perhaps a physical transformation.

His mission: honor the man, the mythic character he originated and their combined legacy. (Weathers died in 2024 at 76.) Related Stories Emma Chamberlain, Wesley Wang, Aryna Sabalenka and More Unveil New Projects for YouTube Creators Pounce on Midterm Elections, Hoping to Win New Viewers and More Dollars

&#x201C;It's not lost on me, just how important Carl Weathers was not only in this franchise, but what he represented as a young Black leading man during that era,&#x201D; James tells Variety , sitting down for an extensive interview about the role. &#x201C;So, I just wanted to do that person justice and give him as many colors as I could in the short amount of time that I had in this film.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Peter Farrelly's &#x201C; I Play Rocky ,&#x201D; now playing in theaters nationwide, focuses on the unbelievable true story of how Sylvester Stallone (portrayed by Anthony Ippolito) came to write &#x201C;Rocky&#x201D; and ultimately play the title role. But as much as the movie focuses on Stallone's star-making moment, it also spotlights the key casting of Weathers, a former pro football star, who'd played bit parts on shows like &#x201C;Good Times,&#x201D; &#x201C;The Six Million Dollar Man&#x201D; and &#x201C;Kung Fu.&#x201D;

James shines in the character's introduction scene: a crackling sequence in which Weathers auditions to play Apollo Creed, the heavyweight champ whom Stallone's underdog Rocky will fight. James' Weathers struts in with his shirt unbuttoned to reveal impressively toned abs. When the casting director asks his age, he quips: &#x201C;Honey, I'm young as the sun and old as spit. Whatever, you need me to be.&#x201D; It's all going swimmingly &#x2014; he delivers his lines with panache; he's got experience in the boxing ring (a fib, but we'll get to that later) &#x2014; until it's time to read with a mumbling Stallone. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;Look, can we cut?&#x201D; Weathers says, leaping to his feet to complain about his scene partner. &#x201C;I would really do better if I had a real actor reading with me, goddamnit.&#x201D; When he's informed that Stallone is the writer and lead actor of the picture, he replies, slyly: &#x201C;Well maybe he'll get better.&#x201D;

The fine-tuned comedy is a different look for the 32-year-old Canadian star, best known for dramatic parts &#x2014; like &#x201C;If Beale Street Could Talk,&#x201D; &#x201C;Homecoming,&#x201D; &#x201C;The Piano Lesson&#x201D; and &#x201C;Ricky&#x201D; &#x2014; and he plays it all with a mischievous glint in his eye.

&#x201C;He's got so much presence. He's so magnetic that it wasn't hard,&#x201D; James says about filming the sequence. &#x201C;I just tried to step into the best version of myself, tap into all the presence and charm that I have &#x2014; and it's not as much as him &#x2014; but, trying to take what was within me and just compounding on top of it.&#x201D;

While &#x201C;I Play Rocky&#x201D; coincides with the 50th anniversary of the original &#x201C;Rocky,&#x201D; the movie also comes after Creed's legacy has been pushed to the forefront of the franchise thanks to Michael B. Jordan and Ryan Coogler's blockbuster &#x201C;Creed&#x201D; trilogy. During the press run, James joked about calling up his &#x201C;son&#x201D; Jordan (as the Oscar winner's Adonis Creed is the love child of the late boxing champ) to talk about the family business.

&#x201C;I'll tell you the truth: I did not call Mike, and we did not have this discussion,&#x201D; James says, laughing. &#x201C;But, I will say that I'm happy to be in the family.&#x201D;

To prepare for the role, James dropped between 20 and 25 pounds in two months and learned how to box for real. Read on for more about how he prepared for the part and the question he wishes he could've asked Weathers before production.

