Oh OK, cool. If I'm being honest, yeah, there are little white lies that you tell to help set yourself up for success. You don't want to get caught in those lies too, though. So you want to make sure you can sort of deliver on it. Or that by the time they catch you in the lie, they love you so much that it doesn't matter. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Yep, I'll say I ride a horse. I own a horse. I've even put that on my resume. So, you know, whatever you got to do.

See, you believe me. That was good, right?

More than anything, it was just fun. So many times when you're performing, I'll have moments where I'm like, &#x2018;Oh, I can't even be around anyone,&#x2019; or I'm so locked in and so hyper focused on lines, or trying to stay in a in a vibe or a mood. That wasn't this [movie] for me. This was Peter Farrelly giving me the keys to the scene and being like, &#x2018;Go do your thing.&#x2019; So, it was very rewarding to see how it finally turned out.

I just got a call from my manager, like most things, that they're making this movie and that they were looking for Carl Weathers. And I was like, &#x2018;Carl Weathers, yes. Where do I sign up?&#x2019; It didn't take any convincing. I read the script. I was blown away by it. I put my tape together for Pete, and he liked it.

There's an internal litmus test that a lot of actors have. Maybe they'll admit it. Maybe they won't. But a part of it is when you read something and you're like, &#x201C;I don't want to see anyone else do this.&#x201D; Like, &#x201C;I feel like I have the most to add to it or bring to it, and I don't want to see anybody else's version of this. I want to do my version.&#x201D; So, that was a big deciding factor. Just reading it and being like, &#x201C;No, it's too special&#x201D; on the page; I want to be able to do it myself. These characters that mean so much, that are so impactful, it's an honor. It's like why wouldn't I want to have that you know on my belt if you will, that I got to play Carl Weathers. It's amazing! blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid3' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

His warmth was something that people don't really get to see too much. Just looking at him, he could come across as like this physically imposing, maybe scary individual, but I've spoken to people who've spent a lot of real time with him, and you know they've all said just how kind he was.

I tried to add that into the film just in terms of his relationship with Sly. When he finally admits that he's not a boxer, and the fact that they could both laugh at that moment and then bond on something like, &#x201C;Yes, we&#x2019;re adversaries in this film, but, for the purposes of making this film, we're gonna have to lock in and be able to trust each other, and it'd be nice if we liked each other too.&#x201D;

I'd be keen to know if he really understood what he would mean to the legacy of this franchise, not only in the four &#x201C;Rocky&#x201D; films he made, but, if you count the &#x201C;Creed&#x201D; films [too]. The fact that there was a whole other world that spawned off people's love for you and your character and your lineage, that we can make a whole series of movies about his son now.

That really is Carl Weathers and his legacy. Not every actor rather is going to step into that role and last for four movies and then [influence] three more after that. Like, that's because of him. So, I would wonder if he knew on those first days on &#x201C;Rocky I,&#x201D; like, did you ever think it could be this?

I was just over 200 pounds when I found out that I got this job and I found out that I had two months to get ready for this. So, my initial thought process was, &#x201C;Let me just start eating and bulking up,&#x201D; like protein for breakfast, lunch and dinner, just go ham. And I spoke to a trainer friend of mine, and he said, if you work on cutting your body fat percentage down, effectively losing weight while keeping your muscle, you'll be great. And people are gonna think you look bigger than you actually are. Trust me. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid4' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

So, that became my process: weight training at the gym in the morning; going down to Kingsway Boxing Club in Toronto with my trainer Jennifer Huggins and we just took it day by day, step by step. It started with cardio, just getting my endurance level up, then it was footwork. I didn't realize how big footwork was in boxing. Just learning how to not move around like a baby deer. And then unlearning all of those things to be the unpolished version of Apollo Creed. There were layers and levels to it. By the time I was done, I ended up dropping like 20-25 pounds and in the film, I&#x2019;m 170-175 max.

I'm still healing from some of the punches I took, but it was a lot of fun to work with Anthony and spend so much time with him. Just getting close with him, building like a bond and a level of trust with each other. That's crucial, time for character development. For us to actually be going through the motions of the choreography in that last fight scene, getting into the psychology of what it meant to be a boxer and respecting that art form, the process was equally as important as the filming itself.

First of all, I wear like the greatest suits ever, so that's really fly. They're all like custom made, so hopefully the production will give them to me afterward, because like who else are they gonna fit? So that's been really really cool.

